    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28945" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Metilius</span></b> , a, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a Roman family name</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">M. Metilius,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 5,
					11</span></i>
			.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Meti-lius</span></b> , a, um, <i>adj.,
			of</i> or <i>belonging to a Metilius</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Metilia lex,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					35, 17, 57, § 197</span></i>
			.</div>
